} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $8$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $5$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $3$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $8$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+0y=8 \\\\ -3x+4y=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot 4-(-3)\\cdot 0}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3\\text{ } & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-321437/field-1" "q-321437/field-2" "q-321437/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321437"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72738/selection/da0ee6c5caafeec0472285db5df7042eac8fa59edee10830993cfc7e91d49a70" :answer/id #uuid "fe89a93a-2270-5174-821d-e390faba4189" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72738/selection/cf87bc2f3d74814f72c8d451eb7955f5bb0b9c94441c32bd60f073969842f9d9" :answer/id #uuid "480bb830-e354-5f9a-adc3-e262845ca9bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72738/selection/3335b256bd01c2f0480ff65b86b310f959d43e203a41269f4857ec49b10b2465" :answer/id #uuid "b5b6d23b-d0d4-5dbb-8db7-578185802856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72738/selection/70c47c8c6b414ad95000f170fd45538f819d546a296cf50444afae5d22fd3318" :answer/id #uuid "32cce108-ac5b-5fea-8383-f90e3ab8c213" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{4}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72738/selection/6855db5e899c52de82615b07d0bcfd4cf8165a7f2583cd5cc89dd42f91e710e4" :answer/id #uuid "1e7f8a25-1786-52d0-ba03-189387e70a8d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72738/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e698766-c6c7-5110-82a3-cffb299457b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72738/selection/da0ee6c5caafeec0472285db5df7042eac8fa59edee10830993cfc7e91d49a70" :answer-field/choices ["q-72738/selection/da0ee6c5caafeec0472285db5df7042eac8fa59edee10830993cfc7e91d49a70" "q-72738/selection/cf87bc2f3d74814f72c8d451eb7955f5bb0b9c94441c32bd60f073969842f9d9" "q-72738/selection/3335b256bd01c2f0480ff65b86b310f959d43e203a41269f4857ec49b10b2465" "q-72738/selection/70c47c8c6b414ad95000f170fd45538f819d546a296cf50444afae5d22fd3318" "q-72738/selection/6855db5e899c52de82615b07d0bcfd4cf8165a7f2583cd5cc89dd42f91e710e4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72738" :question/id #uuid "ac75f36c-a5e4-5bd7-8fee-5e3a0c9025f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-72738" :question/problem "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-x=3y \\\\ y=-x+1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}-x-3y=0 \\\\ x+y=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)\\cdot 1-(-3)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-72738/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72738"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321438/field-1/7dc57cbcb166e0a2621ef29c6641365f7521881e50652de826ccfa3b3171f3bf" :answer/id #uuid "0420cf23-2175-59ad-8af8-e5a5352e4691" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{35}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321438/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "892f7e39-c35f-5068-9a10-d316cf45943f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :a