--- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ | $-7$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-14$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}0x+7y=-14 \\\\ -5x+2y=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{0\\cdot 2-(-5)\\cdot 7}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -7 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-14 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-321438/field-1" "q-321438/field-2" "q-321438/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4691976a-d825-5f6c-aed7-0d9b45560952"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321438"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4508"] :question/worked-solution "This system can be written as\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080115/assets/843dcd4359e4b61eb9715966fbbe6c26363ab5cfc57c55f94b6a41a73ec7feb1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080115/assets/b9ba240f93ee3ec8c02e9718d62342dca0e0855e24c7b34ed97758a6eb7c46b8.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-4\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the solution is $x=0$ and $y=2.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4509"] :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ -5x+6y=-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $A\\mathbf{x} =\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080115/assets/240a1d2f7f93ec808127c9fa1791a77a43fcd7c0c84505540acc81c8b9fbc6e1.png)\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14080115/assets/7850cbafc78f2cf2ce14ae7111064bf2f5a029f4d1b97b6d5ebfc09e7126f44e.png) This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-3.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
